# Repos whose packages may lag the archive without failing `verify-fresh`.
#
# A repo someone is actively working in builds different bytes than the archive
# holds, every time. That is not a publishing mistake, but the freshness gate
# cannot tell it apart from one — so without this list, shipping any single fix
# means either republishing work in progress or narrowing SUITE by hand, which
# leaves no record of what was skipped.
#
# A held repo is reported as `held` and excluded from the failure count. It is
# NOT excluded from the archive: whatever version the pool already carries stays
# published and keeps being served. Holding a repo pauses re-publication, it
# does not withdraw anything.
#
# One repo directory name per line, as it appears in SUITE without the `../`.
# Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored. Remove a name the moment its work
# lands — a stale hold silently stops the gate doing its job for that repo, and
# the report prints each held repo by name so that is visible rather than
# forgotten.

